STATUS: PLACEHOLDER — generated from src/go.mod only, NOT the resolved
module graph, and license identifiers below are NOT verified against actual
LICENSE file contents in each dependency. This file was assembled without
running any `go` tooling (a hard constraint on how this file was produced —
see src/scripts/generate-notice.sh's header for the tool this project uses
once CI runs it), so:

  * It lists every module path and pinned version declared directly in
    src/go.mod (both the direct and `// indirect` require blocks). It does
    NOT walk the full transitive graph the way `go list -m all` or
    go-licenses would — some modules present only via src/go.sum, or pulled
    in transitively without a go.mod line, may be MISSING from this list.
  * The "License" field for every entry below reads UNVERIFIED. Do not treat
    any license identifier in this file as confirmed until CI has run
    src/scripts/generate-notice.sh and replaced this content — this project's
    own rule (see the PR that introduced this file) is that a wrong license
    claim is worse than a missing one, so nothing here is guessed.
  * No license text is reproduced below, for the same reason: this script
    cannot fetch or verify it without go tooling / module cache access.

CI (.github/workflows/go-security-analysis.yml, job "notice-drift") runs
src/scripts/generate-notice.sh on every change touching src/go.mod,
src/go.sum, or that script, regenerates this file authoritatively via
google/go-licenses against the full resolved module graph, and fails the
build if the committed file differs — see that job for the enforcement, and
src/docs/releases.md for what this file covers and does not cover. The
FIRST such CI run is expected to replace this entire file, including this
notice, with real per-dependency license text; that replacement is the
intended, tolerated way this placeholder stops being a placeholder — the
drift guard is written to require a diff resolve into a "generated by
go-licenses" file, not to require byte-identity with this placeholder
forever. See that job's comments for exactly how it treats first-run drift.

Regenerate locally with a Go toolchain installed:

    src/scripts/generate-notice.sh

Scope: this file is intended to cover Go module dependencies compiled into
the `hive`, `hive-hub`, and `hive-contributor` binaries. It does NOT cover
base-image OS packages or the Node.js/tmux layers built from source in the
container images — those are covered by the per-image SBOMs attached to
every tagged release (see src/docs/releases.md, "Software bill of materials
(SBOM)").

